# The upper wire level: the wire tile's dust lifted to y = 3, each dust on a
# stone at y = 2. A tile carries a lower and an upper wire at once (a stack), so
# two nets cross as two straights, or two turns share a tile, without a climbing
# arm. The stone under the upper dust is what keeps the levels apart: dust only
# weakly powers the block it stands on, which the lower dust cannot read, and a
# conducting block above the lower dust stops it from connecting diagonally
# upward. Only wiring has upper ports, so no lamp or torch is ever beside the
# stone. The build may put a repeater in the arm the signal enters by, as in the
# wire tile; it stands on the stone too.
tile wire_up
size 5 4 5
port W io 0 3 2
port E io 4 3 2
port N io 2 3 0
port S io 2 3 4

legend
  C minecraft:stone
  c minecraft:redstone_wire
  W minecraft:stone if W
  w minecraft:redstone_wire if W
  E minecraft:stone if E
  e minecraft:redstone_wire if E
  N minecraft:stone if N
  n minecraft:redstone_wire if N
  S minecraft:stone if S
  s minecraft:redstone_wire if S

layer 2
  ..N..
  ..N..
  WWCEE
  ..S..
  ..S..
layer 3
  ..n..
  ..n..
  wwcee
  ..s..
  ..s..
